[N 39-40 Razorfen Downs]
[D Forever Shaman 30-60 (Braedyn)\\Razorfen Downs on the Barrens road below the Great Lift: A Host of Evil at the door, Belnistrasz's idol, the Coldbringer's Eye and, if you were 39 in Stormwind, Bring the Light.]
[GA Alliance]
[OC]|cffffffffLevel check|r  -  This chapter wants level 39. Quilboar trash is 34-36 (green), the undead half is 35-40, the bosses 39-40 and Amnennar the Coldbringer a level 41 elite, so a group of five at 38-40 belongs here. Under 38: run it anyway with a group at or above 39 and keep to its pace; there is no later slot (the block has no other Kalimdor visit)
[OC]|cffffffffMyriam Moonsinger|r  -  you arrive from chapter 39 on the Barrens road at the Great Lift's Barrens end, with the Heed My Call ritual done; hearth = Farholde Keep and it stays there, unused. Required chapter: one run of Razorfen Downs, |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, never a re-run. Three quests handed in here (7,985 XP and 75s) plus the Eye and, if you took it, Bring the Light, both handed in later
[OC]|cffffcc00Log check:|r The Coldbringer's Eye (96773, from Lan'dalock in chapter 34); Bring the Light (3636) only if you were level 39 at chapter 39's Stormwind stop; Heed My Call (96135) with the Eye of the Tempest for Veyric (39c); 669 for Seahorn (39c); The Riverglades Report (95315, chapter 40)
[OC]|cffffcc00Sources:|r quest ids, mob and boss levels, drops and item stats come from the Forever DB and the Wowhead Forever tooltips. The Downs' portal, the layout inside, Belnistrasz's spot and the idol event are Classic knowledge, not verified on Forever; the DB has no positions inside the instance, so the pins on dungeon lines point at the door

[OC]|cffffffffAt the door|r  -  Myriam stands by the entrance; the Ratchet flight point (Bragok) is the nearest
At [TAR12866 Myriam Moonsinger], [QA6626 A Host of Evil] [G49.0,94.9 The Barrens]
[OC]|cffffffffRazorfen Downs|r  -  |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r, mobs 34-40 and bosses 39-41 in the DB, one run. Your quests, with the honest label:
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r A Host of Evil (6626) - 8 Razorfen Battleguards, 8 Razorfen Thornweavers, 8 Death's Head Cultists - |cff66ff66normal|r, |cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r: level 33-34 elites that the DB puts only outside the door, so the same five clear them on the way in. 3,450 XP + 75s at Myriam
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Scourge of the Downs (3523) and Extinguishing the Idol (3525) - Belnistrasz inside - |cff66ff66normal|r, but an |cFFFF0000escort: every member must hold the quest|r. 285 + 4,250 XP and the Dragonclaw Ring
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r The Coldbringer's Eye (96773) - |cff66ff66normal|r: the Eye is an object on the ground (Wowhead Forever: 230 of 230 loots from it), not a drop; its spot inside is unverified. 4,100 XP + 55s at Lan'dalock in chapter 39c
[OC]|cffffcc00?|r Bring the Light (3636) - kill Amnennar the Coldbringer - |cff66ff66normal|r, only if it is in your log. 4,300 XP at Archbishop Benedictus in chapter 39d
|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Kill 8 [TAR7873 Razorfen Battleguard], 8 [TAR7874 Razorfen Thornweaver] and 8 [TAR7872 Death's Head Cultist] around the door (level 33-34 elites) [QC6626] [G47.5,91.0 The Barrens]
[OC]|cffffcc00Entrance (unverified):|r beside Myriam, at about 49,95. The DB has two Meeting Stones on this stretch, at 45.2,88.6 and 43.7,90.0; the second stands at Razorfen Kraul's door (chapter 26), so the first is probably the Downs' one
|cFFFF0000GROUP 5|r Meet the group and enter Razorfen Downs [G49,95 The Barrens]

[OC]|cffffffffInside|r  -  quilboar 34-36 in the front half (Withered Warriors, Spearhides, Battle Boars, Reavers, Quilguards, Death's Head Geomancers and Necromancers), undead 35-40 behind them (Splinterbone Skeletons, Warriors, Centurions and Captains; Skeletal Frostweavers and Summoners; Thorn Eaters and Boneflayer Ghouls; Frozen Souls and Freezing Spirits). Bosses: Mordresh Fire Eye 39, Tuten'kash 40, Glutton 40, Lady Falther'ess 40 (event), Amnennar the Coldbringer 41 elite, and two rares that may not show, Ragglesnout 40 and Plaguemaw the Rotting 40
[OC]|cffffcc00Belnistrasz (Classic: early in the instance, unverified):|r every member takes both of his quests before anyone starts the escort
At [TAR8516 Belnistrasz], [QA3523 Scourge of the Downs] (he hands you Belnistrasz's Oathstone) [G49,95 The Barrens]
Speak to [TAR8516 Belnistrasz] again: [QT3523] (285 XP) [QA3525 Extinguishing the Idol] [G49,95 The Barrens]
[OC]|cFFFF0000ESCORT:|r Belnistrasz walks to the quilboar idol and channels while waves of quilboar attack; protect him until the ritual ends (Classic-era, unverified on Forever)
Protect [TAR8516 Belnistrasz] through the ritual at the idol [QC3525] [G49,95 The Barrens]
At Belnistrasz's Brazier, [QT3525] (4,250 XP + Dragonclaw Ring) [G49,95 The Barrens]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Gear (Extinguishing the Idol):|r Dragonclaw Ring (+7 Sta, 5 health per 5 sec) scores nothing on the weights: vendor it (sells for 40s 84c) unless a ring slot is empty
Loot The Coldbringer's Eye from the ground - its spot is unverified, so look along every hall on the way to Amnennar [QC96773] [G49,95 The Barrens]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Mordresh Fire Eye):|r |cff66ff66Deathmage Sash|r (cloth waist +15 Int +7 spell damage, req 36, ~27%) - roll, wear it at once: 39.3 vs Violet Sash 26.9 on the weights. Glowing Eye of Mordresh (neck +8 Int +7 spell damage, req 36, ~37%) beats Giantstone Medallion but not the Triune Amulet - roll only if you have no Triune. Mordresh's Lifeless Skull is an off-hand - pass
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (rares, if they show):|r Boar Champion's Belt (Ragglesnout: mail waist +15 Str +6 Sta, req 37, ~28%) - the second waist after the Deathmage Sash, wearable from 40 (Mail is trained in chapter 39d). Swine Fists (Plaguemaw: leather hands +8 Str +8 Agi, ~34%) are below Traveled Gloves - pass
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (pass):|r Coldbringer Spine (staff, below Bonebiter), X'caliboar (2H sword), Coldrage Dagger and Glutton's Cleaver (one-handers), Icemetal Barbute and Carapace of Tuten'kash (plate), Robes of the Lich, Bonefingers, Fleshhide Shoulders, Silky Spider Cape, Arachnid Gloves, Decaying Flesh Bands, Plaguerot Sprig, Savage Boar's Guard (shield), Lady Falther'ess' Finger (wand)
[OC]|cffffcc00Amnennar the Coldbringer|r (41 elite) is the end boss and wants the full group
Kill [TAR7358 Amnennar the Coldbringer] at the end of the Downs - Bring the Light, only if you took it in chapter 39 [QC3636] [G49,95 The Barrens]
[OC][A Shaman] |cffffcc00Loot (Amnennar):|r |cff66ff66Deathchill Armor|r (mail chest +3 Sta +9 Int +15 Spi +7 spell damage, req 39, ~25%) - ROLL: the best chest on the weights at 40 (66.7 vs Doomsayer's Robe 57.0), but it is mail, so carry it and wear it from 40, after chapter 39d trains Mail
[OC]|cffffcc00Leaving:|r walk out of the Downs. Do NOT hearth: it would put you in Farholde Keep, and Myriam and chapter 39c's road start at the door

[OC]|cffffffffBack at the door|r
At [TAR12866 Myriam Moonsinger], [QT6626] (3,450 XP + 75s) [G49.0,94.9 The Barrens]
[OC]|cffffcc00Check:|r handed in here: A Host of Evil (6626), Scourge of the Downs (3523) and Extinguishing the Idol (3525). In the log for later chapters: The Coldbringer's Eye (96773, complete, to Archmage Lan'dalock in the Dalaran crater in 39c), Bring the Light (3636, complete, to Archbishop Benedictus in Stormwind in 39d) if you took it, Heed My Call (96135) with the Eye of the Tempest (to Veyric, 39c), 669 (to Seahorn in Booty Bay on 39c's way back) and The Riverglades Report (95315, chapter 40). Hearth = Farholde Keep. Next: chapter 39c starts here at the door and rides to Ratchet
